WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.554
Peter danced around the nursery with joy, and Tinker Bell followed his every move.

2
00:00:06.555 --> 00:00:11.099
They ignored Mr. Darling asleep in Nana's dog house.

3
00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:15.214
Peter peeked into the other room to see who was playing the piano.

4
00:00:15.215 --> 00:00:20.073
He whispered to Tink, "That's Wendy's mother.

5
00:00:20.074 --> 00:00:24.604
She's a pretty lady, but not as pretty as Wendy."

6
00:00:24.605 --> 00:00:30.502
All of a sudden, the music stopped, and Peter saw that Mrs. Darling was crying.

7
00:00:30.503 --> 00:00:33.891
Her heart seemed to be broken.

8
00:00:33.892 --> 00:00:38.881
"She wants me to open the window," thought Peter, "but I won't!"

9
00:00:38.882 --> 00:00:45.141
Peter took a step closer and saw the tears shining on her cheeks.

10
00:00:45.142 --> 00:00:49.215
"She's awfully fond of Wendy," he thought.

11
00:00:49.216 --> 00:00:53.332
Then he said stubbornly, "But so am I!"

12
00:00:53.333 --> 00:00:58.884
Mrs. Darling continued to cry, and Peter couldn't look at her anymore.

13
00:00:58.885 --> 00:01:03.455
He skipped about and made funny faces, but this didn't help.

14
00:01:03.456 --> 00:01:06.576
He began to feel sorry for her.

15
00:01:06.577 --> 00:01:11.880
"Oh, all right," he said at last and opened the window.

16
00:01:11.881 --> 00:01:17.947
"Come on, Tink," he called. "We don't want any silly mothers anyway."

17
00:01:17.948 --> 00:01:22.036
And he and Tinker Bell flew out the window again.

18
00:01:22.037 --> 00:01:30.766
When Wendy, John, and Michael arrived, they found the window open, just as Mrs. Darling had left it for them.

19
00:01:30.767 --> 00:01:34.319
They flew in and looked around.

20
00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:37.833
Everything in the nursery looked very familiar.

21
00:01:37.834 --> 00:01:42.014
"I think I've been here before," said Michael.

22
00:01:42.015 --> 00:01:48.858
"Of course you have, silly. There is your old bed," said Wendy, pointing.

23
00:01:48.859 --> 00:01:54.747
"So it is," said Michael, as though he really remembered.

24
00:01:54.748 --> 00:01:59.890
"And look," cried John, "there's Nana's dog house.

25
00:01:59.891 --> 00:02:03.931
Perhaps Nana is in there." He went to look.

26
00:02:03.932 --> 00:02:10.191
"There's a man inside!" he said in a surprised voice.

27
00:02:10.192 --> 00:02:13.661
"It's Father!" cried Wendy.

28
00:02:13.662 --> 00:02:19.126
"Let me look at him," Michael begged. He took a good look.

29
00:02:19.127 --> 00:02:25.951
"He's not as big as the pirate I killed in Neverland," he said with disappointment.

30
00:02:25.952 --> 00:02:31.285
Thankfully, Mr. Darling was still asleep and did not hear him.

31
00:02:31.286 --> 00:02:40.959
"Surely," said John, who had lost faith in his own memory, "Father didn't always sleep in a dog house."

32
00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:45.745
Just then Mrs. Darling started to play the piano again.

33
00:02:45.746 --> 00:02:49.732
"That must be Mother," cried Wendy.

34
00:02:49.733 --> 00:02:54.789
"Then you're not really our mother, Wendy?" asked Michael.

35
00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:59.453
Wendy looked at Michael in a wistful way and patted his head.

36
00:02:59.454 --> 00:03:03.547
"Let's surprise Mother," suggested John.

37
00:03:03.548 --> 00:03:09.174
"We'll put our hands over her eyes and ask her to guess who we are."

38
00:03:09.175 --> 00:03:12.288
Wendy thought they should break the news more gently.

39
00:03:12.289 --> 00:03:16.055
"Let's get into our beds," she suggested.

40
00:03:16.056 --> 00:03:20.745
"We'll be there when she comes in, as if we had never left."

41
00:03:20.746 --> 00:03:28.447
The children all ran to their beds and jumped between the sheets, pulling the covers up to their chins.

42
00:03:28.448 --> 00:03:35.605
When Mrs. Darling went back to the nursery to see if her husband was still asleep, all the beds were filled.

43
00:03:35.606 --> 00:03:40.586
The children waited for her cry of joy, but it didn't come.

44
00:03:40.587 --> 00:03:48.716
She had dreamed so many times that her children were still in their beds that she thought this was just another dream.

45
00:03:48.717 --> 00:03:54.990
As she had often done before, she sat in the chair by the fire and closed her eyes.

46
00:03:54.991 --> 00:04:00.056
The children were disappointed. "Mother!" cried Wendy.

47
00:04:00.057 --> 00:04:05.386
"That's Wendy," said Mrs. Darling, sure it was her dream.

48
00:04:05.387 --> 00:04:08.976
"Mother!" cried John.

49
00:04:08.977 --> 00:04:12.072
"That's John," she said.

50
00:04:12.073 --> 00:04:16.612
"Mother!" cried Michael. He knew her now.

51
00:04:16.613 --> 00:04:19.745
"That's Michael," she said.

52
00:04:19.746 --> 00:04:22.398
Then she opened her eyes.

53
00:04:22.399 --> 00:04:28.546
And all three children jumped out of bed and ran into her arms.

54
00:04:28.547 --> 00:04:34.151
"George, George!" she cried, "The children are back!"

55
00:04:34.152 --> 00:04:39.350
Mr. Darling woke up in the dog house and Nana came rushing in.

56
00:04:39.351 --> 00:04:41.538
It was a beautiful sight.

57
00:04:41.539 --> 00:04:47.141
So beautiful, in fact, that it would have warmed the heart of anyone who looked on.

58
00:04:47.142 --> 00:04:53.971
But no one else was watching, no one except for a little boy staring through the window.

